格式示例（仅结构，不是来源事实）：evidence:[{"paragraph_id":"p3s1","fact":"该片段支持的中文转述"}]。请从本次真实输入挑选编号。","role":"system"},{"content":"{"metadata":{"description":"pi tui style code agent base on deepseek harness","id":"gh:1335566636","install_available":false,"language":"TypeScript","name":"dsh-code","slug":"guoxiucai/dsh-code","topics":["deepseek","deepseek-harness","deepseek-harness-plugin","dsh","dsh-plugin","dsh-plugin-market","dsh-plugins","pi","pi-tui","terminal","tui"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"pi tui style code agent base on deepseek harness"},{"id":"p2s1","text":"dsh-code"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"A DeepSeek Harness terminal coding agent for developers who prefer a focused TUI workflow."},{"id":"p4s1","text":"English · 简体中文"},{"id":"p5s1","text":"> [!IMPORTANT]\n> `dsh-code` is an independent community project, not an official DeepSeek\n> distribu"},{"id":"p5s2","text":"tion. DeepSeek Harness is also in developer preview, so\n> compatibility-breaking upstream changes ma"},{"id":"p5s3","text":"y occur between pinned baselines."},{"id":"p6s1","text":"## Why dsh-code?"},{"id":"p7s1","text":"DeepSeek Harness provides an\nofficial Web UI and a plugin-first agent runtime. `dsh-code` is for dev"},{"id":"p7s2","text":"elopers\nwho prefer to stay in the terminal: it packages the same DSH agent semantics in\na compact, k"},{"id":"p7s3","text":"eyboard-driven interface that works naturally beside shells,\neditors, Git, and remote development en"},{"id":"p7s4","text":"ven interface that works naturally beside shells,\neditors, Git, and remote development environments."},{"id":"p8s1","text":"The product draws on the interaction ideas of\nPi and uses\n`@earendil-works/pi-tui`\nfor terminal rend"},{"id":"p8s2","text":"ering. It does **not** fork or replace the agent core. The Agent\nLoop, sessions, model adapters, too"},{"id":"p8s3","text":"ls, sandbox, permissions, MCP, Skills,\nPlan/Todo, and sub-agents remain owned by the pinned DSH runt"},{"id":"p8s4","text":"sandbox, permissions, MCP, Skills,\nPlan/Todo, and sub-agents remain owned by the pinned DSH runtime."},{"id":"p9s1","text":"In short:"},{"id":"p10s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p11s1","text":"## Requirements"},{"id":"p12s1","text":"| Component | Supported platforms (0.1.6+) |"},{"id":"p13s1","text":"| macOS | 14 or later, Apple Silicon (`arm64`) |\n| Windows | Windows 10 or later, x64 |\n| Linux | x6"},{"id":"p13s2","text":"4, validated on Ubuntu 22.04; Ubuntu 24.04 installation CI |\n| Node.js | `22.19+` (Node 23 excluded)"},{"id":"p13s3","text":" or `24+` |\n| Package manager | npm for normal installation |"},{"id":"p14s1","text":"Linux x64 joins macOS and Windows in 0.1.6. Physical Ubuntu validation is recorded\nin the Linux vali"},{"id":"p14s2","text":"dation report. Linux clipboard support\nrequires `wl-copy`/`wl-paste` (Wayland), or `xclip`/`xsel` (X"},{"id":"p14s3","text":"11); `/web` needs a\ndesktop browser for automatic opening."},{"id":"p15s1","text":"Linux ARM64/Alpine (musl), macOS Intel/Rosetta, Windows ARM, and standalone\ninstallations without No"},{"id":"p15s2","text":"de.js are not supported. Other Linux distributions have\nnot been validated."},{"id":"p16s1","text":"## Installation"},{"id":"p17s1","text":"### npm"},{"id":"p18s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p19s1","text":"Install the current release candidate instead of the stable channel:"},{"id":"p20s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p21s1","text":"Verify the installation:"},{"id":"p22s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p23s1","text":"The scoped npm package is `@tsingwill/dsh-code`; the installed command remains\nthe shorter `dsh-code"},{"id":"p23s2","text":"e scoped npm package is `@tsingwill/dsh-code`; the installed command remains\nthe shorter `dsh-code`."},{"id":"p24s1","text":"### Build from source"},{"id":"p25s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p26s1","text":"## Preview"},{"id":"p27s1","text":"## Highlights"},{"id":"p28s1","text":"- **Terminal-native workflow** — streaming Markdown, five-line collapsed\nreasoning and verbose tool "},{"id":"p28s2","text":"bodies, always-visible line-numbered file diffs,\nselectable/copyable results, themed paste markers, "},{"id":"p28s3","text":"shell blocks, and a\nbottom-pinned composer.\n- **Standard and PTC modes** — Standard makes direct too"},{"id":"p28s4","text":"l calls; PTC composes\nmulti-step work in one TypeScript program. PTC child calls use native tool\nrow"},{"id":"p28s5","text":"s, with long bodies collapsed and file diffs always visible.\n- **DeepSeek Harness semantics** — uses"},{"id":"p28s6","text":" DSH's public session/events and services;\nthere is no second agent loop, session store, permission "},{"id":"p28s7","text":"engine, or tool registry.\n- **Model setup in the TUI** — configure DeepSeek, OpenAI, or an\nOpenAI-co"},{"id":"p28s8","text":"mpatible endpoint through an inline, reversible wizard.\n- **Safe project startup** — canonical-path "},{"id":"p28s9","text":"trust records and `read-only`,\n`workspace-write`, or `danger-full-access` permission presets.\n- **Pe"},{"id":"p28s10","text":"rsistent sessions** — start, resume, search, delete, fork from a historical\nrequest, clone the curre"},{"id":"p28s11","text":"nt snapshot, inspect statistics, and compact context.\n- **Agent visibility and decisions** — dedicat"},{"id":"p28s12","text":"ed Plan/Todo states, queued-user\nmessage feedback, tool progress, retry and compaction indicators, o"},{"id":"p28s13","text":"ne-shot\napproval bars, structured questions, plan review, and a clickable active\nsub-agent indicator"},{"id":"p28s14","text":" with cancel/remove controls.\n- **Fast terminal controls** — slash-command completion, fuzzy `@` fil"},{"id":"p28s15","text":"e and\nfolder completion, direct `!` shell mode, inline selectors, and\nkeyboard-first navigation.\n- *"},{"id":"p28s16","text":"*Independent installation** — stores product data under `~/.dsh-code`, keeps\na separately installed "},{"id":"p28s17","text":"`dsh` command untouched, and supports explicit updates.\n- **Adaptive visuals** — a DeepSeek-blue pal"},{"id":"p28s18","text":"ette tuned independently for dark\nand light terminal backgrounds."},{"id":"p29s1","text":"## Architecture"},{"id":"p30s1","text":"`dsh-code` is deliberately a thin terminal host over a fixed DSH baseline:"},{"id":"p31s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p32s1","text":"The launcher owns only product concerns: command parsing, `~/.dsh-code` home\nisolation, project trus"},{"id":"p32s2","text":"t, session selection, profile initialization, updates,\nand delegation to the upstream DSH executable"},{"id":"p32s3","text":". The TUI renders structured\nevents and sends input back through the public `AgentHandle` API.\nThe T"},{"id":"p32s4","text":"UI exposes only the upstream `standard` (Standard) and `ptc` (PTC) Agent\nPresets. New sessions defau"},{"id":"p32s5","text":"lt to Standard and may select PTC at startup or via\n`/mode` before the first turn. The mode locks wh"},{"id":"p32s6","text":"en that turn starts; resume\nalways reconstructs the preset recorded in the event log, so an existing"},{"id":"p32s7","text":" tool\nhistory never changes schema underneath itself."},{"id":"p33s1","text":"See the accepted architecture decisions in `docs/adr/` and the\nexact upstream revision in `UPSTREAM_"},{"id":"p33s2","text":"ted architecture decisions in `docs/adr/` and the\nexact upstream revision in `UPSTREAM_BASELINE.md`."},{"id":"p34s1","text":"## Quick start"},{"id":"p35s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p36s1","text":"On the first launch for a project:"},{"id":"p37s1","text":"1. Review the canonical project path and choose a permission preset.\n2. If `~/.dsh-code/.credentials"},{"id":"p37s2","text":".yaml` has no saved API credential, dsh-code\nautomatically opens the inline provider setup.\n3. Selec"},{"id":"p37s3","text":"t a provider, save the first API token and default model, then send a\ntask in the editor. Use `/conf"},{"id":"p37s4","text":"ig` later to add or change providers."},{"id":"p38s1","text":"For the official DeepSeek API, `/config` asks for the API key and default model.\nFor an OpenAI-compa"},{"id":"p38s2","text":"tible service, the wizard keeps five explicit values:"},{"id":"p39s1","text":"1. provider route ID;\n2. base URL;\n3. credential environment-variable name (pre-filled from the rout"},{"id":"p39s2","text":"e ID);\n4. API key;\n5. model ID."},{"id":"p40s1","text":"[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p41s1","text":"## Contributing and security"},{"id":"p42s1","text":"- Read `CONTRIBUTING.md` before opening a pull request.\n- Use GitHub Issues for public\nbug reports a"},{"id":"p42s2","text":"nd feature requests.\n- Report vulnerabilities privately as described in `SECURITY.md`.\n- Never attac"},{"id":"p42s3","text":"h unredacted API keys, session logs, credentials, or crash logs."}],"truncated":true}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}
